#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171739 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "104ad420-9a16-51b9-bfc5-16080b22fd49" :question/math-academy-id "e-5108" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2}$." :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{3} \\choose {\\color{blue}2}}$, we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ of Pascal's triangle.\n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0$.\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0$.\n\nThe value located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n1; 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{vmatrix}2\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{vmatrix}3\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮\\end{vmatrix}⋮ \\mid ⋮ \\mid ⋮\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} = 3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171740 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Relationship Between the Rows of Pascal's Triangle in Terms of Binomial Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "587f0594-4911-5ad7-9f1a-bd33cfbad3fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5109" :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n$\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{\\left[\\phantom{3 \\choose 3}\\right]}$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{4} \\choose {\\color{blue}3}}$, we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}4$ and position $\\color{blue}3$ of Pascal's triangle.\n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0$.\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0$.\n\nThe location of $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n(\\frac{0}{0}); (\\frac{1}{0})\\begin{vmatrix}(\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\ (\\frac{2}{0})\\end{vmatrix}(\\frac{2}{1})\\begin{vmatrix}(\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\ (\\frac{3}{0})\\end{vmatrix}(\\frac{3}{1})\\begin{vmatrix}(\\frac{3}{2}) & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\ (\\frac{4}{0}) & (\\frac{4}{1})\\end{vmatrix}(\\frac{4}{2})\\begin{vmatrix}(4 3) & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮\\end{vmatrix}⋮\\begin{vmatrix}⋮ & ⋮\\end{vmatrix}⋮\n$$\n\nNow, $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171741 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "9f9efb07-33a0-5a28-8eef-656a3c00a200" :question/math-academy-id "e-5231" :question/problem "Determine the value of $\\displaystyle{5 \\choose 4}$." :question/worked-solution "The binomial coefficient $\\displaystyle{n \\choose r}$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{n \\choose r} = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\, r!}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n = 5$ and $r = 4$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\frac{5}{4}) &= (5!)/((5 - 4)! \\cdot 4!) \\\\\n&= \\frac{5 \\cdot 4!}{1! \\cdot 4!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5 \\cdot 4!}{1 \\cdot 4!} \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a80404d2-000a-54bd-b6f1-9b7ea113f361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171086} {:answer/id #uuid "d18ea5f3-4264-5b34-b716-0493ec5965e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171087} {:answer/id #uuid "d31df334-4d48-5e8f-9062-892f2449ef55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171088} {:answer/id #uuid "f397885f-c04f-5aad-8ebc-c95d639de0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171089} {:answer/id #uuid "17a657fa-37a1-5087-b7f3-a48d03580bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a80404d2-000a-54bd-b6f1-9b7ea113f361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171086} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b91b72-e763-5535-8591-9d52aee0e0ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171085}] :question/id #uuid "cdf7006a-1c37-5b80-8205-e900efc11d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-69663" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{3}{1})$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Relationship Between the Rows of Pascal's Triangle in Terms of Binomial Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db543b4f-62e6-5781-9acc-bf9f32cbdd78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{0})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171098} {:answer/id #uuid "1894c9e0-2db8-538b-96d7-7bdfd293c739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171099} {:answer/id #u